                                                        <script>
                                                            const faqData = {
                                                                general: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What are Unreal Engine game development services?",
                                                                        a: "Unreal Engine game development services cover any production work carried out inside Unreal Engine, from a gameplay system, art integration, or performance optimization engagement through to a complete UE5 title produced, certified, launched, and supported post-launch by a dedicated external studio."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is the difference between a UE5 specialist studio and a general game development company?",
                                                                        a: "A specialist Unreal Engine game development studio has discipline leads with shipped production experience inside UE5's specific toolchain, such as Nanite, Lumen, GAS, and World Partition."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Why choose UE5 over Unity for a new console or PC title?",
                                                                        a: "Unreal Engine 5 delivers superior out-of-box visual fidelity for console and PC targets, particularly for large open worlds, cinematic-quality characters, and physically accurate lighting through Nanite and Lumen. "
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What makes Clarisco a top Unreal Engine game development company?",
                                                                        a: "Clarisco is recognized among Unreal Engine game development companies for discipline-led depth across UE5's full toolchain, verifiable console certification experience, transparent milestone accountability, and a post-launch retainer model."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Does Clarisco work as an Unreal Engine game development studio for both AAA co-development and indie full-cycle?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our Unreal Engine game development studio delivers both as AAA and AA co-development, where our team embeds into your existing UE5 pipeline, and full-cycle Unreal Engine game development for founders and publishers building a complete title without an internal team behind it."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is the Unreal Engine game development software stack Clarisco works with?",
                                                                        a: "Our Unreal Engine game development software stack covers UE5.3 and UE5.4, Perforce Helix Core for version control, ShotGrid and Jira for production management, Houdini for procedural art pipelines, Unreal Insights for profiling, and platform-native SDK tools for PS5, Xbox GDK, and Nintendo Switch development."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does the Unreal Engine game development interface affect co-development integration?",
                                                                        a: "The Unreal Engine game development interface, including the Editor layout, content browser, output log, and Blueprint visual scripting environment, is the shared workspace our team operates in daily. Our developers configure their Editor environment to match your project's conventions and workflows."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Where can I download or access Unreal Engine for a development project?",
                                                                        a: "Unreal Engine is available as a free download from Epic Games' website at unrealengine.com. Source access and commercial licensing terms apply for specific distribution models. For businesses evaluating Unreal Engine game development download options for a commercial project, our scoping call covers the appropriate licensing path before production begins."
                                                                    }
                                                                ],

                                                                business: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What UE5 systems does Clarisco's Unreal Engine game development team cover?",
                                                                        a: "Our Unreal Engine game development team covers Nanite, Lumen, MetaHuman, Niagara, World Partition, PCG, Gameplay Ability System, Enhanced Input, Mass Entity, Replication Graph, Chaos Physics, Sequencer, nDisplay, and all major platform SDKs across engineering, technical art, and cinematic production disciplines."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can your team work inside our existing UE5 project without disrupting our internal team?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our co-development practice integrates into your Perforce depot, your ShotGrid or Jira pipeline, your code architecture conventions, and your milestone framework by producing deliverables that pass your internal review without requiring your team to adapt their workflow around ours."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Do you handle Unreal Engine console game development and certification?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our console practice covers PS5, Xbox Series X|S, and Nintendo Switch by including first-party SDK integration, platform performance optimization, and full TRC/TCR/LotCheck certification submission management from first compliance run through final platform holder approval."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can your UE5 team handle large open-world development with World Partition?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our engineering and technical art teams have configured World Partition for large open-world environments by covering streaming grid setup, data layer architecture, HLOD generation, level instance organization, and Nanite-based environment art production at world scale."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Do you integrate AI tools into Unreal Engine game development?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. AI tools for Unreal Engine game development we integrate include DLSS 3 and FSR 3 upscaling, XeSS for Intel GPU targets, AI-driven behavior tree NPC systems, PCG automated world population, and machine learning-based animation systems where the project's performance budget supports them."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can Clarisco optimize an existing UE5 project that's missing frame rate targets?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our UE5 performance optimization practice begins with Unreal Insights profiling sessions across target hardware to identify GPU, CPU, and memory bottlenecks, followed by targeted optimization covering Nanite configuration, Lumen performance settings, draw call reduction, Blueprint-to-C++ migration, and asset streaming tuning."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Does your Unreal Engine game development studio handle VR production?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our UE5 XR practice covers Meta Quest 2/3/Pro, PlayStation VR2, and PC VR by handling interaction design, spatial UI, comfort optimization, foveated rendering configuration, and platform submission for immersive experiences across all major headset targets."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What backend services do you integrate with UE5 multiplayer projects?",
                                                                        a: "We integrate UE5 multiplayer titles with Epic Online Services, Steam Online Subsystem, Xbox Live, PlayStation Network, custom Node.js backends, AWS GameLift for dedicated servers, and PlayFab for economy, cloud saves, and live-service event management."
                                                                    }
                                                                ],
                                                                pricing: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How much does Unreal Engine game development cost?",
                                                                        a: "Unreal Engine game development cost depends on platform target, visual fidelity requirement, feature scope, and production model. AA indie console titles typically range from $200K–$1M+. AAA co-development engagements scale by discipline and team size. Full-cycle UE5 mobile titles can start from $80K depending on scope."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How long does a full-cycle Unreal Engine game development project take?",
                                                                        a: "A typical UE5 mobile or indie title runs 20–32 weeks. AA console productions typically run 12–24 months. AAA co-development engagements are scoped per milestone commitment. A week-by-week production plan is agreed before week one, with clear milestone gates and exit criteria confirmed before production begins."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is a typical Unreal Engine game development team size for a co-development engagement?",
                                                                        a: "Unreal Engine game development team size for a Clarisco engagement typically ranges from 4 to 50+ specialists depending on scope, from a focused engineering co-development team of 4–8 through to a full multi-discipline co-development team covering art, engineering, technical art, and QA simultaneously."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What does the Unreal Engine game development workflow look like for a new engagement?",
                                                                        a: "Our UE5 workflow runs in eight stages: Technical Architecture Scoping → Pre-Production & GDD → Prototype & Vertical Slice → Full Production → QA, Optimization & Certification → Soft Launch or Beta → Global Launch → Post-Launch Support."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How quickly can Clarisco's UE5 team integrate into our project after signing?",
                                                                        a: "Our Unreal Engine game development team configures to your Perforce depot, project management tools, and milestone framework within five to seven business days and produces first committed deliverables by the end of week two faster than most UE5 vendor onboarding timelines."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Who owns the UE5 project files and source code after the engagement?",
                                                                        a: "All Unreal Engine project files, C++ source code, Blueprint assets, Niagara particle systems, Material instances, and build configurations transfer entirely to you at project completion. No licensing fees and no retained rights."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How is a UE5 co-development engagement priced?",
                                                                        a: "Co-development engagements are priced as time-and-materials or milestone-tied fixed-scope depending on deliverable definition clarity at project start. Full-cycle engagements are priced per phase and discipline with cost confirmed before signing. We provide a detailed estimate document before any contract discussion begins."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Do you offer a trial sprint for UE5 co-development before a full commitment?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. For clients validating team quality before a full engagement, we offer a two-to-four-week trial sprint with agreed UE5 deliverables and defined review criteria allowing both teams to confirm integration fit and output standard before the full engagement contract is signed."
                                                                    }
                                                                ]

                                                            };

                                                            function createFaq(section, id) {
                                                                const container = document.getElementById(id);
                                                                faqData[section].forEach((item, index) => {
                                                                    const html = `<div class="accordion-item">
                                                                        <p class="accordion-header">
                                                                        <button class="accordion-button ${index !== 0 ? 'collapsed' : ''}" 
                                                                        data-bs-toggle="collapse" 
                                                                        data-bs-target="#${section}${index}">
                                                                        <span class="faq-icon"><i class="bi bi-book"></i></span>
                                                                        <span class="faq-title">${item.q}</span>
                                                                        </button>
                                                                        </p>
                                                                        <div id="${section}${index}" class="accordion-collapse collapse ${index === 0 ? 'show' : ''}"  data-bs-parent="#${id}">
                                                                        <div class="accordion-body">${item.a}</div>
                                                                        </div>
                                                                        </div>`;
                                                                    container.insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend", html);
                                                                });
